		(descr "Standex DIP05-1A72-13L reed relay, PIN-OUT CODE 13, RENUMBERED for tscircuit dip4 authoring: coil COIL_A=1/COIL_B=2 (west column), contact CONTACT_B=3/CONTACT_A=4 (east column). Isolation boundary between the columns, 7.62 mm (ADR-0002) -- and under code 13 that statement is TRUE. Physical DIP-14 lead positions: COIL_A=DIP2, COIL_B=DIP6 (both west), CONTACT_A=DIP14, CONTACT_B=DIP8 (both east), per DS p.3 Pin-Out sub-figure 13. REPLACES pinout12, where the leads are 1/14 and 7/8 tied as two CONTACT nodes with the coil on inner pins -- that land shorted 5V_KEY_RELAY to the select bus and gave the coil no holes at all.")
